// The link checker's own service (L-ITEM, SPEC-v3 3.4; links SPEC section 6).
// The checker runs on an officer's own machine and calls in through the edge
// with its client-credentials token (the linkcheck client, scope links.check).
// The API refuses its token on every other service, and every other token on
// this one. No request here carries a bytes field (the untrusted-pdf gate).
//
// What it sees: web and mail addresses only, never a piece's text, a link's
// words or a title. It may be given an address from a members-only passage or
// an officers-only item, so each list handed out is audited (links_read, at
// the officers' audience).
//
// What it may do: record a verdict on an address it was given. It cannot
// accept a link that needs a sign-in to check, cannot answer for a reviewer,
// and cannot change, add or re-enable an address.
//
// L5's ListPublishedLinks and ReportLinkCheck join this service later.

